      "worked_solution": "To calculate ${\\color{red}3} \\div \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}$, we need to divide each of $\\color{red}3$ wholes into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129499/assets/327833c4954c43c2093cb31a03cef01e66389e7cafc3bb2d4cd174e0f7e64f5d.png)\n\n \n\nWe get ${\\color{red}3} \\times {\\color{blue}5} = 15$ pieces in total. \n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n3 \\div \\dfrac{1}{5} = 15\n$$",
